  "steps": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a heavy pot or tagine over medium-high heat. Season the lamb with salt and pepper, then brown it in batches until well coloured on all sides. Remove and set aside.",
    "Add the onion and carrot to the pot and cook for 6 to 8 minutes, stirring often, until the onion softens and starts to turn golden. Stir in the garlic, cumin, coriander, paprika, cinnamon, and turmeric for 1 minute until fragrant.",
    "Return the lamb to the pot. Add the canned tomatoes and vegetable stock, scraping up any browned bits from the bottom.",
    "Bring to a simmer, cover, and cook gently for about 75 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the lamb is tender.",
    "Stir in the dried apricots and honey, then cook uncovered for 10 to 15 minutes until the sauce thickens slightly and the apricots are plump.",
    "Meanwhile, toast the almonds in a dry pan for 3 to 4 minutes until golden and aromatic.",
    "Finish the tagine with lemon juice and most of the parsley. Taste and adjust the seasoning, then scatter over the toasted almonds and remaining parsley before serving."
